From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:41:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ec/lenovo/h8: Power on with AC, keyboard beep, USB charge on
 battery

The OEM firmware of the ThinkPad W541 (GNET94WW) has three EC settings
in its setup that coreboot lacks or gets wrong. Its EcIoDxe reads them
from the LenovoConfig variable and sets bits in the EC config bytes,
which h8_enable() writes from the devicetree at every boot:

- Power On with AC Attach: EC 0x01 bit 1, set when on. The EC powers
  the laptop on when AC is plugged in, and resumes it from hibernation.
- Keyboard Beep: EC 0x03 bit 1, set when off: the beep of the EC for a
  key combination that it does not handle.
- Charge in Battery Mode, under Always On USB: EC 0x02 bit 3, set when
  off, and set whenever Always On USB is off. The W541 devicetree has
  config2 = 0xa8, with the bit set, and h8_usb_always_on_enable() only
  writes EC 0x0d, so "AC and battery" most likely acts as "AC only" in
  hibernation and power-off on battery. Upstream once set this bit for
  AC only (b21f5d708af) and dropped it in a rewrite (4f4322dd685).

Three new chip flags, has_power_on_ac_attach, has_keyboard_beep_option
and uao_battery_in_config2, make h8_enable() set those bits from the
options power_on_ac (default off), keyboard_beep (default on) and
usb_always_on, which clears bit 3 only for "AC and battery". Only the
W541 devicetree sets them, and its defaults give the bytes it writes
today (0x05, 0xa8, 0xc4). Every other H8 board writes config1-3 as
before; the T440p has the same config2 = 0xa8, but its OEM firmware has
not been looked at, so it keeps the AC-only behaviour on purpose.

The two new options are in ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.c, suppressed without their
flag and listed in the generic H8 forms too. The W541 menu has them in
Energy Saver > Power and General > Sound. Where config2 bit 3 follows
the option (h8_has_uao_battery_in_config2(), the W541), the help of
"USB always on" says what each value does in hibernation and power-off.
It says nothing about sleep on battery, which the OEM help says still
has power with "AC only"; that is left to the hardware test. The other
boards keep the old help, as the devicetree value of the bit decides
there.

A W541 that already has "AC and battery" chosen powers the port on
battery in hibernation and power-off from this change on, which runs
the battery down; the release notes have to say so.

The EC keeps these bits only while it has power, and a slot built
without this change writes the old bytes again after a vboot fallback.
The OEM firmware also writes EC 0x05 = 0x87 where the devicetree has
beepmask1 = 0x86; whether that bit gates the keyboard beep is an open
point for the hardware test, as are the OEM writes of EC 0x02 bit 7 and
EC 0x03 bits 5-6, which this change does not follow.

TEST=Host syntax check of h8.c, h8 cfr.c and the haswell cfr.c with the
W541 mrc and nri configs and a T440p one; sconfig accepts the new
registers. tools/cfr-dump.sh for mrc and nri: the menu is valid with
both options shown and the W541 help of usb_always_on, every help line
under 60 columns; with the T440p devicetree both are suppressed and
usb_always_on keeps its old help. For the W541 hardware test, first dump
EC 0x01-0x05 and 0x0d (ec_sys) with each usb_always_on value. Power on
with AC attached: off, unplug AC, plug it: the laptop starts, and
resumes from hibernation; off, nothing. Keyboard beep off and on, with
an unhandled Fn combination, also with beepmask1 = 0x87. "AC and
battery": a load on the yellow port has power in power-off on battery;
"AC only": none. The S3 result is to be recorded, not judged. With
power_on_ac on: unplug AC, suspend to S3, plug AC in, and record
whether the laptop wakes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.c                        | 57 ++++++++++++++++-
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.h                        |  2 +
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/chip.h                       | 10 +++
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/h8.c                         | 61 ++++++++++++++++++-
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/h8.h                         |  8 +++
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c            |  2 +
 .../haswell/variants/w541/devicetree.cb       |  4 ++
 7 files changed, 140 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.c b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.c
index 64701a8041..75eb4e5a8a 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.c
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.c
@@ -93,7 +93,23 @@ const struct sm_object h8_cfr_backlight = SM_DECLARE_ENUM({
 	.values		= kic_values_both,
 }, WITH_CALLBACK(update_backlight));
 
-/* USB Always-On */
+/*
+ * USB Always-On. Where config2 bit 3 follows the option (the W541), "AC and battery"
+ * also powers the port on battery in hibernation and power-off; elsewhere the
+ * devicetree value of that bit decides, so the help does not promise it.
+ */
+static void update_usb_always_on(struct sm_object *new)
+{
+	if (h8_has_uao_battery_in_config2())
+		new->sm_enum.ui_helptext = "Power to the Always On USB port while the laptop sleeps,\n"
+					   "hibernates or is off, to charge devices.\n"
+					   "AC only: in hibernation and power-off, only with the\n"
+					   "AC adapter attached.\n"
+					   "AC and battery: in hibernation and power-off on battery\n"
+					   "too, which runs the battery down.\n"
+					   "Default: Disabled.";
+}
+
 const struct sm_object h8_cfr_usb_always_on = SM_DECLARE_ENUM({
 	.opt_name	= "usb_always_on",
 	.ui_name	= "USB always on",
@@ -107,7 +123,7 @@ const struct sm_object h8_cfr_usb_always_on = SM_DECLARE_ENUM({
 				{ "AC only",		UAO_AC_ONLY		},
 				{ "AC and battery",	UAO_AC_AND_BATTERY	},
 				SM_ENUM_VALUE_END				},
-});
+}, WITH_CALLBACK(update_usb_always_on));
 
 /* Ultrawideband */
 static void update_uwb(struct sm_object *new)
@@ -206,6 +222,41 @@ const struct sm_object h8_cfr_battery_beep = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.default_value	= true,
 }, WITH_CALLBACK(update_beep));
 
+/* Keyboard beep, as the OEM setup of the W541 has it (config3 bit 1) */
+static void update_keyboard_beep(struct sm_object *new)
+{
+	if (!h8_has_keyboard_beep_option())
+		new->sm_bool.flags = CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS;
+}
+
+const struct sm_object h8_cfr_keyboard_beep = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.opt_name	= "keyboard_beep",
+	.ui_name	= "Keyboard beep",
+	.ui_helptext	= "Beep of the EC when a key combination that it does not\n"
+			  "handle is pressed.\n"
+			  "Default: on.",
+	.default_value	= true,
+}, WITH_CALLBACK(update_keyboard_beep));
+
+/* Power on with AC attached, as the OEM setup of the W541 has it (config1 bit 1) */
+static void update_power_on_ac(struct sm_object *new)
+{
+	if (!h8_has_power_on_ac_attach())
+		new->sm_bool.flags = CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS;
+}
+
+const struct sm_object h8_cfr_power_on_ac = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.opt_name	= "power_on_ac",
+	.ui_name	= "Power on with AC attached",
+	.ui_helptext	= "The EC powers the laptop on when the AC adapter is\n"
+			  "plugged in while it is off, and resumes it from\n"
+			  "hibernation. The EC keeps the setting while it has power:\n"
+			  "after the battery and the AC adapter were both gone, it\n"
+			  "applies again from the next boot.\n"
+			  "Default: off.",
+	.default_value	= false,
+}, WITH_CALLBACK(update_power_on_ac));
+
 /* Fn-CTRL Swap */
 const struct sm_object h8_cfr_fn_ctrl_swap = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.opt_name	= "fn_ctrl_swap",
@@ -266,6 +317,7 @@ __cfr_form static const struct sm_obj_form cfr_power = {
 	.obj_list = (const struct sm_object *[]) {
 		&h8_cfr_first_battery,
 		&h8_cfr_usb_always_on,
+		&h8_cfr_power_on_ac,
 		NULL
 	},
 };
@@ -301,6 +353,7 @@ __cfr_form static const struct sm_obj_form cfr_misc = {
 		&h8_cfr_volume,
 		&h8_cfr_pm_beeps,
 		&h8_cfr_battery_beep,
+		&h8_cfr_keyboard_beep,
 		NULL
 	},
 };
diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.h b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.h
index b67c97ef4c..b9e89cf999 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.h
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/cfr.h
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@ extern const struct sm_object h8_cfr_wlan;
 extern const struct sm_object h8_cfr_wwan;
 extern const struct sm_object h8_cfr_pm_beeps;
 extern const struct sm_object h8_cfr_battery_beep;
+extern const struct sm_object h8_cfr_keyboard_beep;
+extern const struct sm_object h8_cfr_power_on_ac;
 extern const struct sm_object h8_cfr_fn_ctrl_swap;
 extern const struct sm_object h8_cfr_sticky_fn;
 extern const struct sm_object h8_cfr_f1_to_f12_as_primary;
diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/chip.h b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/chip.h
index 4ac686ea2d..c3547fabd5 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/chip.h
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/chip.h
@@ -35,6 +35,16 @@ struct ec_lenovo_h8_config {
 	bool has_power_management_beeps;
 	bool has_uwb;
 
+	/*
+	 * Settings of the OEM setup that the EC keeps in its config bytes, as
+	 * the OEM firmware of the ThinkPad W541 programs them (EcIoDxe). Only
+	 * boards that set these get the options; the others write config1-3
+	 * as the devicetree has them.
+	 */
+	bool has_power_on_ac_attach;	/* config1 bit 1: power_on_ac */
+	bool has_keyboard_beep_option;	/* config3 bit 1: keyboard_beep */
+	bool uao_battery_in_config2;	/* config2 bit 3: usb_always_on on battery */
+
 	u8 bdc_gpio_num;
 	u8 bdc_gpio_lvl;
 
diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/h8.c b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/h8.c
index 52c02ef8ef..a2e8e0d4d9 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/h8.c
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/h8.c
@@ -332,6 +332,42 @@ bool h8_has_power_management_beeps(void)
 	return conf && conf->has_power_management_beeps;
 }
 
+/* Returns true when the board has the power_on_ac option (config1 bit 1) */
+bool h8_has_power_on_ac_attach(void)
+{
+	const struct device *dev = DEV_PTR(lenovo_ec);
+	assert(dev && dev->chip_info);
+	const struct ec_lenovo_h8_config *conf = dev ? dev->chip_info : NULL;
+
+	return conf && conf->has_power_on_ac_attach;
+}
+
+/* Returns true when the board has the keyboard_beep option (config3 bit 1) */
+bool h8_has_keyboard_beep_option(void)
+{
+	const struct device *dev = DEV_PTR(lenovo_ec);
+	assert(dev && dev->chip_info);
+	const struct ec_lenovo_h8_config *conf = dev ? dev->chip_info : NULL;
+
+	return conf && conf->has_keyboard_beep_option;
+}
+
+/* Returns true when usb_always_on also sets config2 bit 3 (charge on battery) */
+bool h8_has_uao_battery_in_config2(void)
+{
+	const struct device *dev = DEV_PTR(lenovo_ec);
+	assert(dev && dev->chip_info);
+	const struct ec_lenovo_h8_config *conf = dev ? dev->chip_info : NULL;
+
+	return conf && conf->uao_battery_in_config2;
+}
+
+/* A bit of a config byte, from a setup option */
+static u8 h8_config_bit(u8 reg8, u8 bit, bool set)
+{
+	return set ? reg8 | bit : reg8 & ~bit;
+}
+
 static void h8_enable(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct ec_lenovo_h8_config *conf = dev->chip_info;
@@ -356,9 +392,30 @@ static void h8_enable(struct device *dev)
 	reg8 = conf->config1;
 	if (conf->has_thinklight || conf->has_keyboard_backlight)
 		reg8 = (reg8 & 0xf3) | (backlight << 2);
+	/* The EC powers the laptop on when AC is attached */
+	if (conf->has_power_on_ac_attach)
+		reg8 = h8_config_bit(reg8, H8_CONFIG1_POWER_ON_AC,
+				     get_uint_option("power_on_ac", 0));
 	ec_write(H8_CONFIG1, reg8 & ~conf->config1_reserved_mask);
-	ec_write(H8_CONFIG2, conf->config2);
-	ec_write(H8_CONFIG3, conf->config3);
+
+	/*
+	 * Set, the Always On USB port has no power on battery in hibernation and
+	 * power-off: only "AC and battery" clears it.
+	 */
+	reg8 = conf->config2;
+	if (conf->uao_battery_in_config2) {
+		const bool battery = get_uint_option("usb_always_on", UAO_OFF) ==
+				     UAO_AC_AND_BATTERY;
+		reg8 = h8_config_bit(reg8, H8_CONFIG2_UAO_NO_BATTERY, !battery);
+	}
+	ec_write(H8_CONFIG2, reg8);
+
+	/* Set, no beep for a key combination that the EC does not handle */
+	reg8 = conf->config3;
+	if (conf->has_keyboard_beep_option)
+		reg8 = h8_config_bit(reg8, H8_CONFIG3_KBD_BEEP_OFF,
+				     !get_uint_option("keyboard_beep", 1));
+	ec_write(H8_CONFIG3, reg8);
 
 	/*
 	 * Reset LEDs to power on state.
diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/h8.h b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/h8.h
index 0ef285cbf7..49fa4add5d 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/h8.h
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/h8.h
@@ -52,6 +52,10 @@ bool h8_has_uwb(void);
 
 bool h8_has_power_management_beeps(void);
 
+bool h8_has_power_on_ac_attach(void);
+bool h8_has_keyboard_beep_option(void);
+bool h8_has_uao_battery_in_config2(void);
+
 /*
  * boards needing specific h8-related inits could override it
  */
@@ -67,14 +71,18 @@ void h8_mb_init(void);
 
 #define H8_CONFIG1 0x01
 #define H8_CONFIG1_BKLT_LID		0x01
+#define H8_CONFIG1_POWER_ON_AC		0x02	/* W541 EcIoDxe: Power On with AC Attach */
 #define H8_CONFIG1_UBAY_PWR		0x20
 
 #define H8_CONFIG2 0x02
 #define H8_CONFIG2_USB_DOCK			0x01
 #define H8_CONFIG2_DOCK_SPEAKER_MUTE		0x02
 #define H8_CONFIG2_DOCK_SPEAKER_MUTE_POL	0x04
+/* W541 EcIoDxe: Charge in Battery Mode off, Always On USB not on battery */
+#define H8_CONFIG2_UAO_NO_BATTERY		0x08
 
 #define H8_CONFIG3 0x03
+#define H8_CONFIG3_KBD_BEEP_OFF		0x02	/* W541 EcIoDxe: Keyboard Beep off */
 #define H8_CONFIG3_STICKY_FNLOCK_LED	0x10
 
 #define H8_SOUND_ENABLE0		0x04
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index c48f540a87..50b4fb7dbe 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -303,6 +303,7 @@ static const struct sm_object general_sound = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
 		&h8_cfr_pm_beeps,
 		&h8_cfr_battery_beep,
+		&h8_cfr_keyboard_beep,
 		&h8_cfr_volume,
 		NULL
 	},
@@ -426,6 +427,7 @@ static const struct sm_object energy_power = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	.ui_name	= "Power",
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
 		&h8_cfr_usb_always_on,
+		&h8_cfr_power_on_ac,
 		&power_on_after_fail,
 		NULL
 	},
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/variants/w541/devicetree.cb b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/variants/w541/devicetree.cb
index 14b2f4fa4d..2c7e265605 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/variants/w541/devicetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/variants/w541/devicetree.cb
@@ -74,6 +74,10 @@ chip northbridge/intel/haswell
 					register "config2" = "0xa8"
 					register "config3" = "0xc4"
 					register "has_keyboard_backlight" = "1"
+					# The EC settings of the OEM setup (EcIoDxe)
+					register "has_power_on_ac_attach" = "1"
+					register "has_keyboard_beep_option" = "1"
+					register "uao_battery_in_config2" = "1"
 					register "event2_enable" = "0xff"
 					register "event3_enable" = "0xff"
 					register "event4_enable" = "0xd0"
-- 
2.47.3

